      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1171912929,
      "text": "Cymbopogon flexuosus, also called Cochin grass, East-Indian lemon grass or Malabar grass, is a perennial grass native to India, Sri Lanka, Burma, and Thailand. It is placed in the genus Cymbopogon (lemongrasses)."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Cymbopogon flexuosus",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cymbopogon_flexuosus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 121486198,
      "text": "Cymbopogon flexuosus es una planta herbácea perenne natural de la India, Sri Lanka, Birmania y Tailandia, del género Cymbopogon de la familia Poaceae."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Cymbopogon flexuosus",
